response:
The report details cyber attacks targeting local self-government bodies in Ukraine, linked to the threat actor group UAC-0001 (APT28). The attackers utilized phishing emails referencing a Google Sheet theme, directing victims to a fake reCAPTCHA page that induced them to execute a malicious PowerShell command via the Windows Run dialog. This executed an HTA payload (browser.hta) and a PowerShell script (Browser.ps1) aimed at browser credential theft, establishing reverse SSH tunnels, and executing a Metasploit payload (zapit.exe). Command and control infrastructure centered on the compromised server mail.zhblz.com (203.161.50.145), which was also linked to prior exploitation of Roundcube vulnerability CVE-2023-43770 (incident CERT-UA#10859).

